9. Key Implementation Details (for Developer Reference)
========================================================

expandCosting.deluge (Costing Section A auto-expansion):
  - Trigger: On Submit (Costing_Sheet, status Draft)
  - SO System Lines × System Composition (FG per sqm)
  - Section A lists FG Products (not Raw Materials)
  - Costing based on FG roll-up rates from BOM
  - For each FG: fgQty = round(Area × Qty_Per_Sqm, 1)
  - fgRate = Σ(BOM_Ratio × RM Standard_Rate)
  - Creates Costing_Material_Lines with FG data

planReleaseAutoPR.deluge (Plan Released → auto-PR):
  - Trigger: On Record Modified (Production_Plan, Plan_Status → Released)
  - Plan lines are FG products; RM requirement derived via BOM roll-up
  - Stream B PR carries Project ID; Stream A stock PRs carry none
  - De-dupe: only one submitted PR per (Project_ID, RM_Code)

mrDerive.deluge (MR auto-derive from Costing + Plan):
  - Trigger: On Record Modified (Production_Plan, Plan_Status → Released), criteria: Costing Approved
  - MR created as Draft; MIS comes later at Release
  - Zero manual entry — all 4 cost components pre-filled
  - Costing Section A is FG-based; MR allocates RM via BOM roll-up
  - rmAllocMap aggregates RM qty per RM code across all FG lines
  - Creates Material_Allocation rows with Assigned_Qty, Rate, Material_Cost, Allocation_Ratio_Percent
  - 4 cost components: Material + Application + Transport + Tools (Section E excluded)

mrChangeHistory.deluge (MR Change History + Notification):
  - Trigger: On Record Modified (MR_Master) — any field change
  - Logs change to MR_Change_History subform
  - Sends email to Production and Inventory departments
  - Includes formatted HTML table of all changes

